recommend keep-going the next mechanical lap needs no word and is a measured list: readlink -f at 4 real sites and sed -i at 4, each wanting one helper in shell_portable.sh. One question rides with readlink and is worth naming before the lap rather than during it -- two of its four sites (tools/ag/agent-jail.sh, tools/p/pier_nixos_track.sh) are Linux-only by construction and can never run on the second pier, so whether the family reads past a host-bound script or repairs it anyway is a shape decision this round did not make. Every remaining open red is Keaton's: %230 and %252 want the row-number ruling, %248 the integration word with four packages now parked behind it, %255 the send-order choice.
